        "Content": "3 bedroom semi-detached house extending to approximately 98.42 sq. m (1,059 sq. ft)\r\n\r\nLady’s Cross is a very popular development within Clonakilty because of it’s spacious well built houses, well kept communal green areas and convenient location next to all the amenities that the Town has to offer. The subject house itself has an excellent situation within the development opposite a communal green in a cul-de-sac and with a west facing rear garden.\r\n\r\nThe house comes to the market in fair condition. The ground floor consists of a Hall, living room, wc and large kitchen/diner which provides access to the rear garden.\r\n\r\nThe first floor consists of a family bathroom and 3 bedrooms, one of which is a master ensuite. A nice additional feature of the house is the fully floored attic space accessed by stira stairs. The attic has been constructed with future conversion in mind, offering excellent potential to provide additional accommodation.\r\n\r\nThe west facing rear garden is laid out in lawn and features mature trees. There is convenient side access to the front of the property. To the front, there is off-street parking, with a communal green area opposite providing additional parking spaces.\r\n\r\nIt is less than 500m to the N71 National Road which connects Cork City with Bandon, Clonakilty and all the way west to Kenmare in Co. Kerry.\r\n\r\nThe vibrant heritage town of Clonakilty is renowned for its welcoming community and excellent range of amenities, including schools, healthcare services, supermarkets, boutique shops, cafés, award-winning restaurants, hotels and a wealth of independent local businesses.\r\n\r\nCork International Airport is 45 minutes away and Cork City Centre 50 minutes.\r\n\r\nThere are many Beautiful natural amenities including Inchydoney, Long Strand, Castlefreke Forest Trail, Owenahincha, The Warren, Red Strand, Blind Strand, Broadstrand to name a few that are only a short drive away.\r\n\r\nServices: Mains Water & Sewerage, Oil Fired Central Heating\r\n\r\nDisclaimer: All information provided is to the best of our knowledge but is not guaranteed and should be independently verified. No warranties or representations are made regarding the accuracy, completeness, condition or planning status of the property. Interested parties should satisfy themselves as to the correctness of all information provided, including measurements, boundaries, size or acreage, BER details and services. All measurements and distances are approximate and for guidance only. Photographs and video are for illustrative purposes and may include items not included in the sale (e.g. furniture)."
      },
